OL,3,AResidents warned not to drink tap water
OL,4,Aafter hundreds fall sick near South
OL,5,AAfrica capital
OL,6,
OL,7,FResidents living near South Africa's
OL,8,Fcapital, Pretoria, have been warned not
OL,9,Fto drink or cook with tap water after
OL,10,Fmore than 400 people, mostly children
OL,11,Funder four, fell ill after drinking
OL,12,Fcontaminated water.
OL,14,FThe cases were detected in Tshwane, the
OL,15,Farea which includes Pretoria, after
OL,16,Fpeople reported to their local hospital
OL,17,Fwith "stomach cramps and diarrhoea"
OL,18,Fover a two-week period, officials said.
OL,20,FNo deaths have been reported but high
OL,21,Flevels of E. coli were found in the
OL,22,Fwater.
OL,23,APub: 20-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,319,300,200,140,0,100
